    "description": "Nexus Water Group is a regulated water and wastewater utility platform formed through the combination of Corix Infrastructure's U.S. regulated water and wastewater business and SouthWest Water Company. The platform serves residential, commercial, and municipal utility customers through owned water distribution, wastewater collection, and treatment systems. Nexus reported at launch that it employed more than 1,300 professionals serving more than 1.3 million people across North America through over 670 water systems and over 360 wastewater systems, with local operations across 20 U.S. states and two Canadian provinces. The merger closed on April 1, 2024, and BCI's 2024 I&RR financial statements disclose a 50.0% ownership interest in Nexus Water Group Inc. Nexus announced asset-sale agreements with American Water in 2025 and California Water Service Group in 2026, but the company stated the Nevada/Oregon sale was expected to close by the end of 2026 following required regulatory approvals, so BCI's Nexus holding remains active as of May 12, 2026.",
